# Supabase project settings — Project Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Ollie the AI chess coach — falls back to a local knowledge base if no
# provider below is usable. Production default: leave OLLIE_AI_PROVIDER
# unset and just set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (this is the exact prior behavior,
# unchanged). To develop without Anthropic credits, set
# OLLIE_AI_PROVIDER=development and GEMINI_API_KEY instead — Google's free
# AI Studio tier (https://aistudio.google.com) needs no billing account.
# OLLIE_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic | development | fallback (optional)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Required for the Days 4+ paywall to work — Stripe Dashboard > Developers > API keys
# Use a TEST MODE secret key (starts with sk_test_) during development.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# Required for the Stripe webhook (app/api/stripe/webhook/route.ts) to verify
# requests actually came from Stripe. For LOCAL dev, run `stripe listen
# --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook` (Stripe CLI) and use the
# whsec_... value it prints. For production, create a webhook endpoint in
# the Stripe Dashboard pointing at your real domain and use ITS signing secret.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# Required for the webhook to upgrade accounts server-side (it has no user
# session to work through) — Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API >
# service_role key. Keep this OUT of anything that reaches the browser; it
# bypasses all Row Level Security.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Optional, LOCAL DEV TESTING ONLY — set to "true" to:
#   - auto-sign-in as a dedicated dev-only test account (no login screen)
#   - skip the /parent-gate math-challenge screen
#   - show a small "DEV TEST MODE" quick-nav badge
#   - enable /dev/premium-preview (UI-only, no real premium state)
# The auto-sign-in needs that test account to actually exist first — run
# `node scripts/dev-seed-test-user.js` once (uses SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# above). Only works when NODE_ENV === "development"; a production build
# can't activate any of this regardless of the value (see
# lib/devTestMode.ts — verified against the compiled output, not just
# reasoned about). Leave unset for normal behavior (real Supabase sign-in,
# real Parent Gate).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_TEST_MODE=true
